\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Go not, my soul, in search of Him,
\par Thou wilt not find Him there,
\par Or in the depths of shadow dim,
\par Or heights of upper air.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For in far-off realms of space
\par The Spirit hath His throne:
\par In every heart He findeth place,
\par And waiteth to be known.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thought answereth alone to thought,
\par And soul with soul hath kin;
\par The outward God he findeth not,
\par Who finds not God within.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And if the vision come to thee
\par Revealed by inward sign,
\par Earth will be full of Deity,
\par And with His glory shine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thou shalt not want for company,
\par Nor pitch thy tent alone;
\par The indwelling God will go with thee,
\par And show thee of His own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O gift of gifts! O grace of grace,
\par That God should condescend
\par To make thy heart His dwelling-place
\par And be thy daily Friend !
\par \i\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\i0 
\par }

